@startuml
title Soundzone - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Frontend (Browser)" as FE {
  component "React App" as React
  component "Redux Store\n& Actions" as Redux
  component "Playback Manager" as Playback
  component "Audio Player" as Audio
  component "Waveform UI" as Waveform
  component "Forms & Validation" as Forms
  component "Config\n(API base URL,\nCloudinary URL,\nUpload Preset)" as FEConfig
}

package "Backend (Node/Express)" as BE {
  component "Express Server" as Express
  component "Auth API" as AuthAPI
  component "Sound API" as SoundAPI
  component "Follow API" as FollowAPI
  component "Feed API" as FeedAPI
}

database "PostgreSQL" as PG
cloud "Cloudinary\n(Media Storage)" as Cld

' Internal frontend relationships
React --> Redux : dispatch/actions
Redux --> React : state/selectors
React --> Forms
React --> Waveform
Playback --> Audio
Waveform --> Playback : waveform click -> seek
Redux --> Playback : current playback state
FEConfig --> React : runtime config

' Frontend to backend APIs
React --> AuthAPI : HTTP/JSON via API base URL
React --> SoundAPI : create/read/delete sound\n(persist Cloudinary URLs)
React --> FollowAPI : follow/unfollow
React --> FeedAPI : followed users' sounds

' Direct media upload
React --> Cld : direct upload (audio/image)
Cld --> React : hosted URL

' Backend relationships
Express -[hidden]-> AuthAPI
Express -[hidden]-> SoundAPI
Express -[hidden]-> FollowAPI
Express -[hidden]-> FeedAPI

AuthAPI --> PG : users, sessions
SoundAPI --> PG : sounds, media URL refs
FollowAPI --> PG : follow relationships
FeedAPI --> PG : queries for feeds/lists

note right of Playback
- Maintain single current playback
- Preserve playback across navigation/component switches
end note

note bottom of Cld
Store audio/image assets.
Return URLs used by backend persistence.
end note

note bottom of PG
Persist application records and Cloudinary URL references.
end note

@enduml
